<Root>
  <DefaultMacro>
    <Major>AFK Farming In Albion</Major>
    <Description>You can set the positions manually and farm ore, hemp, trees, and stone.

It's recommended to use Borderless Fullscreen mode, or set your resolution to 1366×768. Borderless Fullscreen offers the best experience.

First, find a group of three or more nearby resources. Then, set a position on each resource:

Click on the first resource to set a position.

Click on the next one to set another position.

Repeat until all desired positions are set.

You can adjust the delay time based on your gathering tool’s speed. If your tool gathers faster, reduce the delay; if it gathers slower, increase the delay.

To calculate the delay, check how long it takes to fully gather a resource and add 4 seconds.
Example: If it takes 5 seconds to gather, then 5 + 4 = 9 seconds should be your delay value.

If you’re gathering multiple types of resources, you can set different delay values for each one.
To add more gathering positions, copy the first 8 lines of code.
To remove positions, delete 8 lines from either the top or bottom.

If the Cancel key in your game isn’t set to S, you can either delete or change that keybinding in the script.
If you choose to delete it, make sure to increase the delay time by 6 seconds to maintain accuracy.

Thanks for reading — I appreciate it!</Description>
    <Comment>https://keyran.net - Free macros download | Скачать бесплатные макросы </Comment>
